================================================================================================
CHAT-SIDE UNIFORM CONSTANT C_c: sup over P subset {1..13} of [E_c(H)*H] and #jumps(1_{G_P}).
    [the small part P lives in {1..13} (LRC<=13 routing) => FINITELY many 1_{G_P}.]
================================================================================================
   scanned 2379 subsets P of {1..13} (|P|=1..5).
   sup #jumps(1_{G_P}) = 64  at P=(10, 11, 12, 13)  (FINITE => Vc uniform)
   sup_P E_c(14)*14 = 2.70051  at P=(1, 6, 8, 9, 10)
   sup_P E_c(28)*28 = 3.73826  at P=(10, 11, 12, 13)
   sup_P E_c(56)*56 = 3.27980  at P=(8, 10, 11, 12, 13)
   sup_P E_c(112)*112 = 3.58160  at P=(10, 11, 12, 13)

   => C_c := sup_P sup_H E_c(H)*H ~ 3.73826 (BOUNDED, uniform over P): chat tail energy <= C_c/H.
      lcm(1..13) = 360360; breakpoints of 1_{G_P} have denom | 14*lcm(P), FINITE.

================================================================================================
SUMMARY -- THE UNIFORM CONSTANTS
================================================================================================
  c_core (bounded atlas, EXACT)  = 416640/779291 = 0.534640  >> m_P (=14249/252252=0.056487)
  C_c   (chat tail-energy rate)  ~ 3.73826   (E_c(H) <= C_c/H, UNIFORM over P subset {1..13})
  WIDE side: SPEC -> 0 under dilation => R' -> 1 (eta(V*) -> 0); so wide R' >= 1 - eta(V*).
  H-FREE cap: Var(1_S) <= 1/4 => |sum_high| <= 1/4 for ALL (P,E), ALL H (trivially uniform).

  THE UNIFORM c:  R' >= c := min( c_core , 1 - eta(V*) ).
    - bounded core: c_core is an EXACT rational min over a finite atlas (the consec/binding floor).
    - wide: eta(V*) is the cross-scale decay (SPEC->0 at rate ~span0/V*), -> 0 as V* grows.
    The CS-tail C/sqrt(H) is uniform ONLY on the finite bounded atlas (sup of finitely many C_g);
    the wide regime is NOT covered by a single H-rate (E_g(H)*H unbounded) and instead uses
    scale-separation R'->1 (mac-mini S32).  This is the honest, correct uniform statement.
DONE.
